prompts.base:
ALFWorld is a text-based household environment. At the start of an episode the agent is told which receptacles it can see in the room (for example cabinets, drawers, countertops, shelves, a fridge, a microwave, a sinkbasin, a stoveburner, a garbagecan, a desklamp), each with a number. Objects lie on or inside receptacles, and closed receptacles must be opened to see inside. The agent acts with text commands: go to [receptacle], open [receptacle], close [receptacle], take [object] from [receptacle], put [object] in/on [receptacle], clean [object] with [receptacle], heat [object] with [receptacle], cool [object] with [receptacle], use [object], examine [object or receptacle], look, inventory. An episode has a limited number of steps.

Task type '{task_type}': {goal}

Write {n} concise, GENERAL rules (heuristics) that would help an agent solve this task type. Each rule: one imperative line, no specific object numbers or room layouts. Output ONLY a bullet list, each line starting with '- '.

